//! World generation sweep against Vanilla (#223): compares whole areas generated by Vanillite's
//! chunk generator with the same areas generated in-process by Vanilla's code
//! (`tools/extractor/.../golden/WorldSweep.java`, which documents the file format).
//!
//! Ignored by default; `cargo xtask worldgen sweep` records the Vanilla areas and runs it with
//! `VANILLITE_SWEEP_DIR=<dir with *.bin.gz>` and `VANILLITE_SWEEP_REPORT=<markdown file>`.
//! `VANILLITE_SWEEP_VERBOSE=<n>` prints the first n differing blocks of each area,
//! `VANILLITE_SWEEP_LINES=<n>` lists n other differences per area (default 25) and
//! `VANILLITE_SWEEP_FILTER=<text>` compares only the files whose name contains the text.
//!
//! Both sides run the same pipeline: structure starts, references, biomes and terrain on
//! demand, then the features of every chunk of the area plus one ring, row-major (z outer). The
//! area's chunks are compared as decorated (no light, mob spawning or post-processing): block
//! states, biomes, the four final heightmaps, post-processing marks, scheduled ticks, structure
//! starts (pieces by type, box, orientation and depth), structure references and block entities
//! with their NBT (loot tables and seeds included). Flat worlds use the flat world preset.
//!
//! Known limit (#300): an area that differs only because of a 1-ulp `Math.sin/cos` difference
//! (it matches Vanilla once one ulp-sensitive result near the differences is shifted by 1 ulp,
//! see `vanillite_worldgen::mth::math_sin`) is listed as a known limit and does not fail.

mod common;

